From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:03:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: a waiting subagent's card keeps its prompt and
 follows the subagent

0072 gave SubagentStatus a Waiting variant for an ACP child that reports
requires_action, so the sidebar, the tray and the card can tell a child
waiting for the user apart from one that works. Two checks upstream wrote as
`status == Running` then read Waiting as "stopped", and no patch touched them.
Found by the upstream-native review of 2026-11-15
(docs/UPSTREAM-NATIVE-REVIEW.md in the hub, defect 1).

  - The card embeds a child's pending permission prompt only while the child
    runs. Claude Agent (Plus) reports requires_action before each permission
    request of a child, so the prompt left the parent's card exactly while it
    was pending; the awaiting-permission bar and the child's own view still
    reached it, one click away.
  - Full screen opens a stopped card at the start of its part and a running
    one at the latest entries. A waiting card opened at the start.

SubagentStatus::is_live (Running or Waiting) answers both, as 0072's own doc
comment says Waiting is "live work, not an ending". The embedded prompt gets a
debug selector, subagent-card-permission-{entry}, so a test can see it.

Tests: rfd_surfaces_tests' test_rfd_waiting_child_shows_its_permission_in_the_card
and waiting_card_full_screen_follows_the_latest_entries (both Red on the
series before this patch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/subagent_card.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/subagent_card.rs
index c20387c..fa052c0 100644
--- a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/subagent_card.rs
+++ b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/subagent_card.rs
@@ -164,6 +164,13 @@ pub(crate) enum SubagentStatus {
 }
 
 impl SubagentStatus {
+    /// Running, or waiting for the user: work that has not ended. Upstream's checks read
+    /// `== Running`, which R5.2's `Waiting` would otherwise turn into "stopped" exactly while
+    /// a child waits on a prompt (0132).
+    pub(crate) fn is_live(self) -> bool {
+        matches!(self, Self::Running | Self::Waiting)
+    }
+
     /// An ACP subagent's status from the state it last reported, with the error to show for a
     /// failure. Only an explicit successful stop reason warrants a success indicator.
     pub(crate) fn from_reported_state(
@@ -337,8 +344,7 @@ impl SubagentCardState {
     /// once its work has stopped, or `None` while it runs, so the subagent's view keeps
     /// following its latest entries.
     pub(crate) fn fullscreen_entry(&self) -> Option<usize> {
-        (self.status != SubagentStatus::Running)
-            .then(|| self.entries.map_or(0, |entries| entries.start))
+        (!self.status.is_live()).then(|| self.entries.map_or(0, |entries| entries.start))
     }
 
     /// The last `max_entries` of the entries this card covers.
